body:
Hello,

We are building a more mobile friendly version of our filters and therefor we want to create collapsable filter boxes. Since we are already using Bootstrap 3 at our site I wanted to use their collapse functionality.

When I add the needed html via jQuery to the instantsearch generated html it doesn't work. It seems that it isn't picking up the click event.

When I add this:

```
this.addEventListener("click", function(){ 

            $($(this).data('target')).collapse('toggle');
        });
```

The collapse part works, but it seems that instantsearch is no longer picking up the events.. 

You can see what I mean at https://markputs.nl/algolia.php (make your screen small, javascript can be found in Algolia.js)

Thanks.

comments.body:
@Maaark I had a look right now, I can see the collapsible option seems not to work in your case. Could you try to first update instantsearch.js to the latest version? Your are using an old version (1.6.x), we are at 1.8.x.

Then if it's still not working I would advise you to try to reproduce the bug in a isolated simple webpage first, it will help you understand what can go wrong.

> And is it possible to make the collapsable functionality work with predefined window width limits? So for example we want to be the refinement lists only collapsable when the window width is < 768px?

Once the collapsible option is working in a simple webpage, you should try using our predefined CSS classes to apply some CSS media queries on top of them so that the widget are collapsed only based on the viewport.

See our CSS file (https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/instantsearch.js/1/instantsearch.css):

``` css
.ais-root__collapsible .ais-header {
  cursor: pointer;
}

.ais-root__collapsed .ais-body, .ais-root__collapsed .ais-footer {
  display: none;
}
```
